DESCRIPTION                   =  "The first Stokes parameter, defined as S1 =
|ERH| + |ERV|, represents the total power or total intensity of the received
field. The second Stokes parameter, defined as S2 = |ERH| - |ERV|, represents
the difference between the horizontally polarized intensity and the
vertically polarized intensity. The third and fourth Stokes parameters are
defined as S3  = 2 Re ERH ERV* and S4 = -2 Im  ERH ERV*, respectively. They
jointly represent the real and imaginary phase difference between the
horizontally and vertically polarized components of the recieved field."

